    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a2">

                <pb facs="0244" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg224"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    note of the 19th instant, transmitting to me some printed copies of a.notice
                    issued by the proper authorities, prohibiting vessels coming up above a certain
                    point of the Thames with powder or combustibles, without special permission from
                    the admiralty.</p>
                <p>I shall take pleasure in complying with your request that I should communicate
                    the same to my government, and I shall likewise transmit a copy at once to the
                    consul of the United States at this port.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
